1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,040
Most of us know

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:03,720
that movement and exercise
are good for our physical health,

3
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:05,000
and science is showing

4
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,960
that they're also good
for our mental health.

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,680
But did you know that exercising
with friends comes

6
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:11,560
with its own unexpected benefits?

7
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,880
If you're the type of person
who likes to go to the gym,

8
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:16,560
put on some headphones and
kind of focus on your own thing,

9
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,640
this idea might seem a bit strange.

10
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:22,080
What difference could exercising
with other people actually make?

11
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,520
I feel like it's just so nice

12
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,000
to have the support of your friends

13
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,760
and your team-mates and everything,

14
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,000
and just having people cheer you on.

15
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,520
Everybody cheers behind you
and gets behind you and goes,

16
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:33,440
"Come on, you can finish it!
Last 500m!" and you know,

17
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,560
you know you're going to make it.

18
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,760
Humans evolved
as a social species.

19
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:41,320
Being around our friends makes us
feel safer and less cautious.

20
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:44,640
And this can change
how our bodies respond to exercise.

21
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,160
Fatigue evolved to protect us
from overexertion and injury.

22
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,720
It works like a brake mechanism
that tells us when we need to stop,

23
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:55,080
but it also limits our endurance.

24
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:57,920
When our social environment tells us
we're safe and supported,

25
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,240
our bodies can ease
that protective break.

26
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:03,320
So, by making us feel less fatigued
and more energised,

27
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:05,040
exercising with family and friends,

28
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:06,640
or even just as part of a group,

29
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:08,840
can actually boost
our physical performance.

30
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:13,640
To show this, we ran an experiment
with 25 teenage rowers

31
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,440
here at the Fulham Reach Boat Club.

32
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:18,760
We asked them to row at a set pace
for as long as they could

33
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,640
in two different
social environments.

34
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:23,560
One was designed to make them feel
socially supported,

35
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:26,120
and the other was meant
to make them feel on their own.

36
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:29,280
We found that those who felt
supported got tired less quickly

37
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:32,000
and were able to row
for a longer amount of time.

38
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,600
You see everyone else
row next to you,

39
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,640
you can sort of just zone in

40
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:36,080
and realise that you're not
the only one,

41
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:38,400
and also you have each other
cheering you on, of course.

42
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:41,040
Whilst you're on your own,
it's just really miserable, I guess.

43
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:43,520
In the boat with other people,
there's a sense of camaraderie

44
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:45,320
which you don't have in the boat
by yourself.

45
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:47,320
But on top
of boosting our performance

46
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,480
and making our workouts feel
a bit easier,

47
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:52,120
there's another major benefit
to group exercise.

48
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:54,320
You kind of have
that social aspect,

49
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,600
so it kind of gives you
a mental health benefit

50
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,880
by coming out to the runs.

51
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,360
I think the social activity-

52
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,600
I mean, I've got so many friends now
because of it,

53
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:03,760
and I think
that's one of the big bonuses.

54
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:06,520
And do a run
and a coffee and cake afterwards.

55
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,960
So it's just... Yeah, it's great.

56
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,080
Scientific research
is beginning to show

57
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:12,120
that the more we exercise
with our friends,

58
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,400
the closer we feel to them.

59
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:16,560
Evolutionary anthropologists
call this social bonding.

60
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:19,720
This happens because our bodies
release chemical messengers called

61
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:22,120
endorphins and endocannabinoids
during exercise,

62
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,120
which make us feel happy
and content.

63
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:27,080
You might have heard people saying
they give us a runner's high.

64
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,840
This natural high can help us
be more positive and in tune

65
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:32,880
with the people we're exercising
with, and this helps us feel closer

66
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:34,360
and more connected to one another.

67
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,520
And it turns out
these social connections

68
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:38,680
don't just disappear after exercise.

69
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:41,680
We followed over 50 teams
of teenagers who took part

70
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:44,040
in a challenge which required them
to navigate

71
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:46,480
a difficult 50-mile course
over two days.

72
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:49,840
Teams who reported working together
and supporting one another said

73
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:52,200
they felt closer and more connected
when they finished.

74
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:56,600
What we found really interesting
was that these feelings

75
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:59,920
of social connection positively
impacted their mental wellbeing

76
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,440
a whole week after the event.

77
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:03,160
Again and again, studies have shown

78
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,560
that social relationships
are really important

79
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:06,800
for our overall health.

80
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:09,320
When we feel lonely,
we get more stressed,

81
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,960
and this fight or flight response

82
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,880
is our body's way
of protecting itself

83
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:15,680
from the dangers our ancestors faced
when they were alone.

84
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,280
But in the modern world,

85
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,800
this stress response
can be a bit counterproductive.

86
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:23,200
And when loneliness causes us
to feel chronically stressed,

87
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,280
it can be harmful
to our long-term health.

88
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:28,000
One study even found
that lacking social connection

89
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:30,920
can be as dangerous for our health
as smoking cigarettes.

90
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:33,560
So by exercising together,
we're helping to build

91
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:37,560
the social relationships we need
to live happy and healthy lives.

92
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,280
When I'm here,
I'm not stressed about exams.

93
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:41,720
I'm not stressed about, like,
all of the other things I have.

94
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:43,920
Like, it's just rowing
and I'm just here with my friends.

95
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,040
But what happens

96
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,760
if you don't have family and friends
nearby?

97
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,240
Maybe you've just moved,
or maybe you can be a bit shy

98
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:51,320
and you're not sure
where to meet people.

99
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:54,200
It turns out there are a lot
of exercise groups and clubs

100
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:57,360
that are happy to get new members,
even if you're just getting started.

101
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:00,280
In fact, some are even specifically
for beginners.

102
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,160
I found the group on Facebook,

103
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,600
and it was set up as an event,

104
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:06,000
so I just clicked "going".

105
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,560
I was really nervous about it,
going for the first time,

106
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:11,400
worried about meeting new people,
but they were so welcoming,

107
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:14,600
there wasn't really anything
to worry about, really.

108
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:16,640
And if you can't do
intense exercise,

109
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:18,680
finding a partner
to go on light walks with

110
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:21,160
can also have positive effects
on your health.

111
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:24,560
In fact, any kind of
physical activity that we can do

112
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,600
in collaboration with other people,

113
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:29,480
so things like dancing, gardening
or singing,

114
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:32,760
can help us move more
and feel more socially connected.

115
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:36,600
Public health experts have described
rising levels of physical inactivity

116
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,440
and loneliness as two new epidemics

117
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,040
that are harming our physical
and mental health.

118
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:43,000
It turns out that exercising
together,

119
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:45,400
or even just being active
with other people,

120
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:47,040
might help to cure both.

